In this folder we will create checkers to be sure that all stimulii were creted correctly

1. Topoplots look like targets
Visual check: each generated topoplot should clearly resemble its intended target pattern.
For this we will plot in pdf all and 30 selected topplots. 

search_stimuli.jl

2. Topoplots are diverging over zero

The color range should be centered around zero, for example (-max(abs(values)), +max(abs(values))).
search_stimuli.jl

3. Rereferencing is correct

After average rereferencing, the mean of the new voltage values across channels should be approximately zero for each subject/timepoint/condition.

debug_rereferencing.jl

4. SNR shows influence of both SE and signal

Check that SNR is not only determined by signal amplitude. Even a small SE influence is enough if weak-signal and high-SNR regions can differ. This may be more visible on smaller grid regions.

debug_sss.jl (signal, se, SNR) - topoplots
debug_sss_peaks.jl - table with peaks
debug_sss_peaks_by_regions.jl - table with region peaks
debug_sss_peaks_topo.jl - panel-7-style region-score topoplots for estimate vs SNR

5. All indvidaul plots are plotted correctly for all cases

debug_plots.jl

6. Check pypeline

Check every step of pypeline in which se adn signal are transformed into regions and scores

7. Scores match interpretation

If I select the regions with the highest scores, I should get the regions with the best expected results according to the intended interpretation.
